A||||8||batboy||Batty Fiero taillights||||1||
Z||000000||batboy||01-15-2000||09:36 PM||||Monkeyman was very nice to me and sent one of his famous vinyl stick-on taillight mods. Hmmm, I wonder why he's sucking up to me?<P>I started working on it by disassembling the taillights and cleaning everything. The trim below the taillights was getting shabby, so I masked it off, sanded it lightly, and hit it with some spray can Rustoleum black.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/taillightparts.jpg">  <P>Monkey warned me 2 or 3 times to be careful about sticking the vinyl on because you have only one chance. Well...the inside of the clear outer taillight lens is slightly curved making it almost impossible to apply the vinyl without getting some air bubbles trapped and an occasional crease. Looks a little bit tacky up close, but looks great from a slight distance and fantastic at night.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/batlites.jpg">  <P>Fussy Fiero owners with mint cars might not want to do this mod, but those with average ordinary daily drivers or playtoys like the Batmobile will find it to be a cheap thrill. <B>I love it!</B> I think it adds an unique personal touch.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://sites.netscape.net/batboybain/bat2M8.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 01-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cooter||01-15-2000||09:40 PM||||A little soapy water sprayed on the adhesive will allow the stickers to be moved and then squeegee out the water when you get them where you want them -I know that you knew that already, but others may not!||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||01-15-2000||09:47 PM||||These are not decals, but rather adhesive backed black vinyl. I plan on trying to use a hair dryer to heat up small areas of the vinyl and to make the adhesive nice and sticky, then try smoothing it all out a little at a time. I used an old beat up pair of taillight lens as a trial. Mama didn't raise no fools. I still think it looks pretty cool, wrinkles and air bubbles and all.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-16-2000||02:15 AM||||batboy--I wasn't trying to suck up to you.  You just had a unique handle (and seemed like a nice guy).  I knew that I was gonna do a standard version and thought that it might be nice to see a more custom version.  (The advertising wouldn't hurt either, IMO.)  I'm glad you like them.<P>Fellow forum members--I still have about 10 of these left at forum member prices ($17US incl. US shipping).  Email me if you're interested.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wolfhound||01-16-2000||07:38 AM||||The dishwashing liquid and water solution Cooter mentioned is the proper proceedure for the vinyl also. <BR> Monkeyman, You need to make you a set with the See no evil, Hear no evil, Speak no evil monkeys:-)||||reg||12
Z||000005||batboy||01-16-2000||08:55 AM||||Good one Wolfie! Wish I knew about that soapy water trick before I put the bats on.||||reg||1
